# Component & Code Patterns

**Entry point:** [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md)

## File Placement
| Type | Location | Example |
|------|----------|---------|
| Screen | `app/game/` | `[id].tsx`, `lobby.tsx` |
| Feature component | `src/features/{feature}/components/` | `ContractView.tsx` |
| Shared component | `src/components/` | `ErrorBoundary.tsx` |
| Design-system primitive | `src/design-system/components/` | `Button.tsx`, `Card.tsx` |
| Hook | `src/hooks/` (shared) or `src/features/{feature}/` | `useAlert.ts`, `useGame.ts` |
| Service | `src/features/{feature}/` | `gameService.ts` |
| Pure logic | `src/features/{feature}/` | `gameLogic.ts` |
| Types | `src/types/` | `index.ts`, `taskPack.ts` |

## Component Rules
- Functional components only (no class components except ErrorBoundary)
- Colocate `StyleSheet.create` at bottom of same file
- Props interfaces defined in same file, named `{Component}Props`
- Use `useHoldToConfirm` hook for press-and-hold interactions (don't reimplement)
- Use `getAvatarDisplay(avatarId)` from `utils/avatarDisplay.ts` for avatar lookups (don't call `getAvatarById` + `getAvatarComponent` separately)

## Hook Rules
- Custom hooks go in `src/hooks/` if shared, or feature folder if feature-specific
- Always clean up subscriptions/timers in `useEffect` return
- Never call Firestore directly from components — go through service functions

## Service Rules
- Pure computation → `gameLogic.ts` (no Firebase imports)
- Firestore I/O → `gameService.ts` (thin wrapper that calls pure logic + writes)
- New constants → `src/constants.ts`
- New types → `src/types/`

## Imports
Always use `@/` for `client/src/` paths (configured in tsconfig, babel, Jest):

```typescript
import { startGame } from '@/features/game/gameService';
import { Button, colors } from '@/design-system';
import { strings } from '@/strings';
import { useAlert } from '@/hooks/useAlert';
```

Screens under `client/app/` import from `@/…`, not `../../src/…`.
